Title: Wingfall
Credit: Written by
Author: Gridlight
Draft date: 2026-08-16
Notes: Demo screenplay for the end-to-end pipeline test. One page, roughly 30 seconds of screen time. Deliberately built to exercise every stage: exteriors for wide plates, one speaking character for voice and lip-sync, heavy SFX and ambience, and a clean three-shot escalation that maps to shot-level generation.

====

EXT. SUBURBAN STREET - DUSK

Wet asphalt. Basketball hoops. A sprinkler ticking over a lawn.

The sprinkler stops. Water hangs, then falls.

A shadow slides across the houses — vast, slow, wrong.

MAYA (30s), grocery bag on her hip, looks up.

MAYA
Get inside. GET INSIDE!

She drops the bag. Oranges roll into the gutter.

EXT. SUBURBAN STREET - CONTINUOUS

The DRAGON drops out of the low cloud, wings cracking like sailcloth. It shears the roofline off a house and keeps going.

Shingles rain down. A car alarm starts, then dies.

MAYA runs. Behind her, the street lights up orange.

EXT. SUBURBAN STREET - CONTINUOUS

The dragon banks hard over the cul-de-sac and comes back around.

Maya reaches a storm drain, turns, and looks up into it.

MAYA (CONT'D)
Oh, you have got to be kidding me.

FADE OUT.
